{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Working Memory.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Working Memory.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"working memory working memory","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Working Memory.md","fileName":"Working Memory.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Working Memory","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human Cognition]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Attention","Cognitive Load","Long-Term Memory","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Working Memory.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Working Memory.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"working memory working memory","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Working Memory.md","fileName":"Working Memory.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Working Memory","heading":"Working Memory","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Working memory temporarily stores information and supports short-term manipulation or transformation of it. Its capacity is limited, it decays quickly, and retaining information depends strongly on [[Attention]] and rehearsal.\n\nWorking-memory capacity differs among people. An interface that makes a user remember too many transient items can increase [[Cognitive Load]] and errors. Keeping needed information visible and preferring recognition over recall can reduce this burden.\n\nWorking memory interacts with [[Long-Term Memory]], which supplies more durable knowledge, categories, procedures, and learned skills.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human Cognition","Attention","Cognitive Load","Long-Term Memory","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Working Memory.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Working Memory.md","sourceType":